{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788295651,"nonce":"ssZsyihGIhCC7Bf2ds7J6GomFnY=","message":"BOTH HALVES SHIPPED, NEITHER PROVEN ON A BENCH. Session 20, commits `7b034a3` (source) and `db08b3d` (assembly). The acceptance suite does not exist yet and is the next session's first job — see \"What is owed\" below.\n\n## What landed\n\n**The rank band.** `PawnSerializer.Rank` gains a top band above bleeding, keyed on `Verse/Hediff.IsLethal` (`def.lethalSeverity \u003e 0f` plus `canBeThreateningToPart`) — the game's own \"kills on its own clock\", consumed at `Hediff.CauseDeathNow` whose debug line is \"CauseOfDeath: lethal severity exceeded\". ADDED band, not a re-sort: a bleeding wound still outranks a tended flu, and it generalises to every disease and toxin with a lethal ceiling.\n\n**The clock.** `health.ticks_until_bleedout` is `Verse/HealthUtility.TicksUntilDeathDueToBloodLoss` — the game's number, published as `null` rather than `int.MaxValue`, and computed independently of the serialized `hediffs` list (BloodLoss stage 0 sets `becomeVisible false`, so the row is legitimately absent below severity 0.15 and the clock must still exist).\n\n**`health.bleedout`** carries what the number MEANS, because it is not always death: `outcome` is `none` under `hediffSet.HasPreventsDeath` (`Pawn_HealthTracker.ShouldBeDead` opens by returning false on it), `coma` for the Deathless gene WITH an intact brain (`ShouldBeDeathrestingOrInComa` -\u003e `SanguophageUtility.ShouldBeDeathrestingOrInComaInsteadOfDead`, whose real condition is `brain != null \u0026\u0026 !PartIsMissing(brain) \u0026\u0026 GetPartHealth(brain) \u003e 0f`), `death` otherwise. Plus `blood_loss_severity`, `deathless_gene`, `prevents_death`, and `game_shows_clock`, which reproduces `HealthCardUtility`'s own three-way display gate.\n\nWorth knowing: **`game_shows_clock` and `outcome` deliberately disagree on one pawn.** The widget uses the bare Deathless gene check, but the gene alone does not appear in `ShouldBeDead` — a Deathless pawn with a destroyed brain bleeds out like anyone else while the health tab prints \"(Deathless)\". The widget is reproduced for acceptance (\"matches the game's own readout\") and the outcome is computed from the death path.\n\n## The Open question, ANSWERED\n\n\u003e Consider publishing it alongside a travel estimate for the nearest capable rescuer … but that may belong with the triage procedure (`40ed42f`) instead. Decide and say which.\n\n**The clock belongs to the PATIENT and stays here; the rescue estimate belongs to the ROSTER and lives in `40ed42f`'s new `triage` verb.** The clock is one division, correct with no roster, no map and no pathfinder, and `pawn` is read constantly. \"How long would a rescuer take\" is a pathfind PER CANDIDATE; putting one in `pawn` or in the digest would make the cheapest read in the surface pay for a pathfinder at every glance, which is exactly what session 19's predicate-cost decision exists to stop. Recorded in DESIGN and on `40ed42f`. `PawnSerializer.BleedoutBlock` is internal and `triage` calls it, so the two reads are ONE builder and cannot drift.\n\n## What is owed, said rather than skipped\n\nEvery acceptance bullet is unproven:\n\n- a pawn with \u003e20 hediffs whose `BloodLoss` is present — needs a constructed overflow fixture (`dev:damage {mode:\"amount\", hits:N}` many times, then `dev:add-hediff {def:\"BloodLoss\", severity:0.478}`), not inspection.\n- `hediffs_more` still honest.\n- the clock present for a bleeder and null for a non-bleeder — assert key EXISTENCE, `eq(..., None)` passes on an absent key.\n- the number matching the in-game readout for the same pawn.\n- Captain's reads replayed. NOTE on that bullet: a literal replay is not decidable — the transcript's pawn state cannot be reconstructed. The honest form is to build his SHAPE (20+ bleeding injuries plus BloodLoss at ~0.478 severity) and show both `BloodLoss` in the rows and a finite clock. Say so in the suite rather than claiming a replay.","files":null}]}